      "Title": "Claude Monet to Frédéric Bazille (333)",
      "Body": "<p><strong>From:</strong> Claude Monet (Étretat) &middot; <strong>To:</strong> Frédéric Bazille (Paris) &middot; <strong>W. ID:</strong> 44</p>\\n<p>Monet writes joyfully from Étretat, describing how inspired he feels by nature, how hard he is working, and how little he misses Paris. Being away allows him to express what he feels in painting more freely, in a more personal way.</p>",
