      "Body": "<p><strong>From:</strong> Claude Monet (Giverny) &middot; <strong>To:</strong> Gustave Geffroy (Paris) &middot; <strong>W. ID:</strong> 2957</p>\\n<p>Artists - Monet arranges plans to meet Geffroy in Paris. Responding to Geffroy&#x27;s remark about La petite fille aux cerises (a painting likely by Renoir according to the auction house), Monet agrees that it is a beautiful painting, but notes that 20 years prior everyone considered it horrible. Wildenstein notes this is Morisot’s Jeune fille cueillant des cerises, but the painting was executed in 1891.</p>",
