      "Body": "<p><strong>From:</strong> Claude Monet (London) &middot; <strong>To:</strong> Alice Hoschedé &middot; <strong>W. ID:</strong> 1624</p>\\n<p>He discusses an &quot;unfortunate affair&quot; involving a Major, likely related to his attempts to get early-release form military service for his son Michel, suggesting that a situation could have been handled better and lamenting missed opportunities to intervene. He also writes about recent health issues. Monet mentions his friend, the artist John Singer Sargent, who visited him and encouraged him to resume painting, though Monet insists he has lost interest in it.</p>",
