      "Body": "<p><strong>From:</strong> Claude Monet (Giverny) &middot; <strong>To:</strong> Etienne Winter, Maurice Winter (Paris) &middot; <strong>W. ID:</strong> 2011</p>\\n<p>Life - Monet thanks Winter, Clemenceau’s secretary, for sharing positive news about Clemenceau’s prostate operation. Wildenstein identifies him as Maurice Winter, whereas IAA notes his name as Étienne Winter. \\nEtienne Winter was Clemenceau’s secretary at L’Aurore in the 1890s and was still his personal secretary by 1908. Maurice Winter was his son, who in 1908 also joined Clemenceau’s cabinet.</p>",
